// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL5_SI_Maros_Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - LetterToTarixus 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3355228941" "A Letter to Tarixus"
// DetailString :
"P3190140694" "This letter is written in a strange script on ancient parchment. As you look, the words shift and change into a language you can recognize:  <br><br>'A dreaded One comes <br>Out of a web of darkness. <br>And Coral abides. <br><br>Broken earthen forms - <br>Shape of men with coral hearts. <br>Red stone brings Mad Steel. <br><br>The Mad Metal speaks. <br>For the Cult of the Shaper, <br>Their souls are mere prey. <br><br>An iron puppet - <br>Strings cut, it falls in battle <br>Calling to it's Lord. <br><br>Beat truth from the Wise. <br>The word said through broken teeth, <br>Is Destruction's name. <br><br>The Mad Metal fight. <br>Hammer fights Claw for power. <br>In mayhem hides Truth. <br><br>The Shaper begins. <br>In the maw of destruction, <br>The battle is joined. <br><br>A dreaded One came, <br>Out of a web of darkness. <br>And Coral abides.' The letters change back to an unreadable script, and you're not really sure you saw them change at all."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - OhmMission 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1278129935" "Ohmtown's mission"
// DetailString :
"P4019252507" "After you rescued the Freakshow Juicer called Ohmtown from the circle of Thorns, he told you: <br><br>'Wassup. I'm Ohmtown, Freak Juicer representin' Talos Island out in Paragon. My main man Drek, he sent me out here to find out what's going down here on Sharkhead. Bunch of our boys is gettin all kinda crazy ideas. Talking 'bout cults and coral and golems and stuff. I just got off the boat, an' was on my way to talk to this Doc Buzzsaw chick, when these Circle psychos jumped me. Started askin' what I knew, which was nothin. 'Least, nothin' yet."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P356527576" "It seems so strange to me now, but I understand the perceived need that everything must have a beginning. So here and now will be the start of this, though this has all happened for a very long time... <br><br>Upon this Island is a wrathful spirit called Tarixus. Perhaps you've worked with him already, perhaps not. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Speak with with this Tarixus, present him with the letter I gave you, and tell him that you and I are working together. Ask him for a task, and he will ask you to battle my own kind. Do so, and you can learn much.</A> <br><br>Tarixus knows me. Once all is clear, he won't have interfered."
// AcceptString :
"P3586114825" "Speak with Tarixus"
// SendOffString :
"P3963226721" "The letter I gave you for Tarixus, let me give it to you now. Now, go to Tarixus. Do the task he asks of you. If you want to understand, pay attention. All of the rest will happen when it does."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL5_SI_Maros_Mission1_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1105420823" "No. You have to move speaking with Tarixus from your future to your past. The movement of events from future to past is the only option you have. I miss that, sometimes."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P856364347" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P439702772" "And what do you bring to Tarixus, {VillainName}? A letter? From a member of the Circle of Thorns. My arcane senses detect no threat. Hold it for me, that I may see it. <br>Maros! I know that name. So, you are working with him. This should prove most interesting. No doubt he sends you to me to ensure that I will not act against him. Then, you may return this answer: <br>I will agree not to interfere with Maros's plans, as long has he does a task for me. Several of his fellows from the Circle of Thorns have gathered in an old mine nearby. No doubt they plan against me. I would see them removed. No, destroyed. Tell that to Maros, tell him that is the price to keep our affairs seperate."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL5_SI_Maros_Mission1_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1854027840" "Defeat Circle in cavern"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1722842126" "I'm fairly certain I told you to do as Tarixus asked. I cannot congratulate you on doing it until it is done. Remember, it's all liner for you. Causes precede conclusions."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2687669435" "The depths of this abandoned mausoleum echo with sounds of scraping metal and cruel laughter."

